        "original_id": "b509d342-14ab-5d22-a122-dfcff8b20a00",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Kettering University, University of New Mexico\n- Places: Flint, Michigan, New Mexico\n- Concepts: cooperative education, experiential learning, research institutions, STEM, business education\n\nFacts:\n- Kettering University was formerly named General Motors Institute of Technology.\n- Kettering University is a private university in Flint, Michigan.\n- Kettering University is based on cooperative education and experiential learning.\n- Kettering University offers bachelor's and master's degrees in STEM and business fields.\n- As of 2012, the University of New Mexico was New Mexico's flagship research institution.\n- As of 2012, the University of New Mexico was the largest post-secondary institution in New Mexico by total enrollment across all campuses.\n- As of 2012, the University of New Mexico was one of New Mexico's largest employers.",
